  "generated_text": "Let's carefully review the solution step-by-step to identify any potential errors and correct them if necessary.\n\n### Step-by-Step Review:\n\n1. **Finding the roots of the quadratic equation:**\n   \\[\n   x^2 - 3x + 1 = 0\n   \\]\n   Using the quadratic formula:\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{(-3)^2 - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 1}}{2 \\cdot 1} = \\frac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{9 - 4}}{2} = \\frac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{5}}{2}\n   \\]\n   Thus, the roots are:\n   \\[\n   a = \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad b = \\frac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{2}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Expressing \\(\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{b}} + \\frac{b}{\\sqrt{a}}\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{a}{\\sqrt{b}} = \\frac{\\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2}}{\\sqrt{\\frac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{2}}} = \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3 - \\sqrt{5}}}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\frac{b}{\\sqrt{a}} = \\frac{\\frac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{2}}{\\sqrt{\\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2}}} = \\frac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3 + \\sqrt{5}}}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Simplifying \\(\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{b}} + \\frac{b}{\\sqrt{a}}\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{a}{\\sqrt{b}} + \\frac{b}{\\sqrt{a}} = \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3 - \\sqrt{5}}} + \\frac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3 + \\sqrt{5}}}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Using the identity \\(\\sqrt{a} \\cdot \\sqrt{b} = \\sqrt{ab} = 1\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\left( \\frac{a}{\\sqrt{b}} + \\frac{b}{\\sqrt{a}} \\right)^2 = \\left( a \\sqrt{a} + b \\sqrt{b} \\right)^2\n   \\]\n   Expanding the left-hand side:\n   \\[\n   \\left( \\frac{a}{\\sqrt{b}} + \\frac{b}{\\sqrt{a}} \\right)^2 = \\frac{a^2}{b} + \\frac{b^2}{a} + 2\n   \\]\n\n5. **Finding \\(\\frac{a^2}{b} + \\frac{b^2}{a}\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{a^2}{b} + \\frac{b^2}{a} = \\frac{a^3 + b^3}{ab}\n   \\]\n   Using the identity:\n   \\[\n   a^3 + b^3 = (a + b)(a^2 - ab + b^2)\n   \\]\n   Substituting \\(a + b = 3\\) and \\(ab = 1\\):\n   \\[\n   a^2 + b^2 = (a + b)^2 - 2ab = 3^2 - 2 \\cdot 1 = 9 - 2 = 7\n  